     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If you are running this app on Windows OS, I think the directory will works. To check it the link is correct, you can simple add a print command under the read.csv line, like &#39;print (head(BVC))&#39;, if you can see some data in R console, then the link is correct. Remember even it&#39;s correct, it only works on your computer because all shiny-server must run on Linux OS. <div><br></div><div>You can create a folder, e.g. Data in under your app directory, and put the csv data file into it, then you can import the data using: </div><div>read.csv(&quot;Data/mydatafile.csv&quot;), This works on all operation systems. </div><div><br></div><div>If the link is correct, which means you can import your data into R, then you need to check the format of &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:17px\">BVC$FECHA</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;, as reported, it said the variable is not in a standard unambiguous format, so you need to check the help document of &quot;as.Date&quot;. </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Good luck. </span></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
