     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, December 29, 2014 5:49:34 AM UTC-5, Huidong TIAN wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">If you are running this app on Windows OS, I think the directory will works. To check it the link is correct, you can simple add a print command under the read.csv line, like &#39;print (head(BVC))&#39;, if you can see some data in R console, then the link is correct. Remember even it&#39;s correct, it only works on your computer because all shiny-server must run on Linux OS. <div><br></div><div>You can create a folder, e.g. Data in under your app directory, and put the csv data file into it, then you can import the data using: </div><div>read.csv(&quot;Data/mydatafile.csv&quot;), This works on all operation systems. </div><div><br></div><div>If the link is correct, which means you can import your data into R, then you need to check the format of &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:17px\">BVC$FECHA</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;, as reported, it said the variable is not in a standard unambiguous format, so you need to check the help document of &quot;as.Date&quot;. </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Good luck. </span></div><div><br>On Wednesday, December 24, 2014 8:07:35 PM UTC+1, Edwin Acuña wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:17px\"> I was wondering if anyone could help me. I am creating an app for analysing stocks. I need to upload the dataset of the stocks but i get errors and since i have not  been able to get it to work.here is my ui.R and server.R. one additional issue, i think  the problem is in the server.R 